{
  "schemaVersion": "tracy-personalize/v1",
  "note": "What tools/personalize.mjs changes on a customer's copy of Tracy Base from the questionnaire answers (seed/questions.json: name · sector · contact). Same five kinds as Tracy Business (D38): `identity` is written exactly from the answers (a missing answer EMPTIES the field, never keeps the demo value); `replace` rewrites the demo brand everywhere; `copy` is prose a model writes for the sector, the demo text being the length reference; `facts` are claims about a real business (counts, prices, years, named clients, named people) and are REMOVED, never invented; `blocks` and `rewrite` let the model redo whole cards and entries for the sector. Values use {name} {NAME} {initials} {phone} {address} {year} {sector}. A contact line the customer did not give (phone, e-mail, address, opening hours: the questions never ask for them) keeps the template's value as a placeholder the customer fills in later (`\"unanswered\": \"keep-demo\"`); a rule with `requires` is written only when every fact it names is given.",
  "settings": {
    "title": "{name}"
  },
  "identity": [
    {
      "collection": "site",
      "slug": "site",
      "field": "brand_name",
      "value": "{name}"
    },
    {
      "collection": "site",
      "slug": "site",
      "field": "not_found_back_label",
      "value": "Back to {name}"
    },
    {
      "collection": "site",
      "slug": "site",
      "field": "social_handle",
      "value": ""
    },
    {
      "collection": "site",
      "slug": "site",
      "field": "social",
      "value": [],
      "from": "social",
      "networks": [
        "instagram",
        "facebook",
        "linkedin",
        "youtube",
        "x",
        "tiktok"
      ],
      "item": {
        "platform": "{network}",
        "url": "{url}"
      }
    },
    {
      "collection": "onepage",
      "slug": "onepage",
      "field": "nav_brand",
      "value": "{name}"
    },
    {
      "collection": "onepage",
      "slug": "onepage",
      "field": "footer_brand",
      "value": "{name}"
    },
    {
      "collection": "contact",
      "slug": "contact",
      "field": "email",
      "value": "{email}",
      "unanswered": "keep-demo"
    },
    {
      "collection": "contact",
      "slug": "contact",
      "field": "email_label",
      "value": "",
      "requires": [
        "email"
      ]
    },
    {
      "collection": "contact",
      "slug": "contact",
      "field": "social",
      "value": [],
      "from": "social",
      "item": {
        "label": "{name}",
        "url": "{url}"
      }
    }
  ],
  "replace": [
    {
      "find": "Tracy Base",
      "with": "{name}"
    },
    {
      "find": "@tracybasedemo",
      "with": ""
    }
  ],
  "copyNote": "Read by Tracy's template readiness check, not by tools/personalize.mjs (TCH #1013, D6 + D7): demoCompanyNames is every spelling of the demo company's name, each renamed by a replace rule above; keptText is demo text kept on purpose (collection/slug for an entry, collection/slug.field for one field). The design system page and the marketing samples page show the template's own design (type scale, colours, spacing, sample layouts), not the business, so their words stay as the template has them and are translated like labels. Every `*image_alt` kept describes a demo picture that stays on the customer's site (this template draws no new pictures: `images` is empty), so the words still match the picture. The one-page footer credit names the template's designer.",
  "demoCompanyNames": [
    "Tracy Base"
  ],
